    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "General Services, Office of",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4192\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the commissioner of general services to sell and\nconvey certain state lands in the borough of Manhattan, county of New\nYork to be used for social services programs, educational programs and\naffordable senior housing\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to permit the sale of property to be used\nfor social services programs, educational programs and affordable\nsenior housing in New York City.\n\nSUMMARY:\n\nThis bill would authorize the commissioner of general services to sell\nand convey 128 East 112th Street, Manhattan, New York to Acacia\nNetwork for $1. The property is to be used for social services\nprograms, educational programs and affordable senior housing and upon\nthe termination of such use the property will revert back to the\nstate.\n\nFurther, this bill provides that the Commissioner of OGS shall not\ngrant such land unless an application is made by Acacia Network within\none year after the effective date of this act.\n\nEFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER:\n\nLand currently owned by the state would be transferred to Acacia\nNetwork.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe property would be used for social services programs, educational\nprograms and affordable senior housing which would of great value to\nthe community.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.6838-A - 2013/2014\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nMinimal\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
